## Backlog (`docs/backlog/`)

**One file per release version** (e.g. `0.7.6-[open].md`). The file body is that version's ship checklist.

### Filename tags

`[draft]` · `[open]` · `[partial]` · `[done]` (in `done/`) · `[canceled]` (in `canceled/`)

Pattern: `{semver}-[{status}].md` — e.g. `0.7.6-[draft].md`

### Body `**Status:**` ↔ filename

| Body status | Filename | Location |
|-------------|----------|----------|
| `draft` | `X.Y.Z-[draft].md` | Version scoped, not started |
| `open` | `X.Y.Z-[open].md` | Actively shipping |
| `partial` | `X.Y.Z-[partial].md` | Release in progress |
| `done` | `X.Y.Z-[done].md` | `docs/backlog/done/` |
| `canceled` | `X.Y.Z-[canceled].md` | `docs/backlog/canceled/` — version dropped, will not ship |

### Lifecycle

```
plan version   →  0.7.6-[draft].md
start release  →  0.7.6-[open].md
in progress    →  0.7.6-[partial].md
shipped        →  done/0.7.6-[done].md
dropped        →  canceled/0.7.6-[canceled].md
```

### Semver (major · minor · patch)

| Level | Semver | Codename? | When to bump |
|-------|--------|-----------|--------------|
| **Major era** | `0.x.x`, `1.x.x`, … | **Theme only** (Tunisia category for the whole era) | New product chapter — e.g. v0 engine, v1 player UX, v2 sync |
| **Minor** | `X.Y.0` | **One codename** per minor open | New arc inside the major era |
| **Patch** | `X.Y.Z` (Z ≥ 1) | **None** — version number only | Next real ship batch inside the arc |
| **Origin** | `0.0.1` | One codename (first ship) | — |

Patch count is **not standardized** — never pad patches to match other arcs.

### Mandatory backlog file sections

Every backlog file body includes (use `—` when empty):

1. **`## Status at a glance`** — immediately after version intro (before RFCs/Issues)
2. **`## Shipped`** — numbered emoji task table (`B*-S*` IDs). **Not** markdown checkboxes.
3. **`## RFCs`** — link, slice shipped, status after this version
4. **`## Issues`** — link, slice shipped, status after this version
5. **`## Migration`** — phase link when a migration slice ships
6. **`## Deferred → next version`** when items slip

Update [RFC README](../../docs/rfc/README.md) and [issues README](../../docs/issues/README.md) **Backlog** column when a version ships.

