## Version ↔ RFC ↔ issue (three layers)

| Layer | Owns | Slips how? |
|-------|------|------------|
| **Backlog** `0.7.6-[open].md` | Which items ship in which semver | Move item to next version file; close old version honestly |
| **RFC** `003-[partial]-….md` | Feature spec + full acceptance | **Same file** — status changes only when implementation state changes |
| **Issue** `018-[open]-….md` | Bug, debt, verifiable sub-work | **Same file** — `[fixed]` or `[canceled]` when done or abandoned |

**Version assignment lives in backlog**, not in RFC/issue filenames. Optional in RFC/issue body: `**Target version:** 0.7.7`.

### Version slip (item not done when release closes)

1. Move old backlog → `done/X.Y.Z-[done].md` with **Shipped** and **Deferred → next version** sections
2. Create/update next backlog (e.g. `0.7.7-[draft].md`) with deferred items
3. RFC/issue stays `[partial]` / `[open]` / `[draft]` — do **not** `[fixed]` or `[canceled]` unless work is done or killed
4. `[canceled]` on backlog = version dropped; `[canceled]` on RFC/issue = will never build/fix

### Partial RFC shipped across versions — do not split

Ship incrementally from **one RFC per feature**. Use slices inside the spec, not new RFC numbers.

**Inside the RFC:**

- `## Components` + `## Acceptance (slice)` emoji task tables — flip row Status when code ships
- Optional `## Slices` prose mapping ID ranges to ship batches

**In backlog:**

- Shipped rows name slice + IDs: `RFC-023: ShellScaffold (R23-C02) ✅`
- Deferred references open row IDs: `R23-A10–A14 device smoke`

**RFC status:**

- Stays `[partial]` until **all** acceptance rows ✅ for that RFC → then `[fixed]`
- Do **not** rename to `[fixed]` because one slice shipped in a version
- Backlog `[done]` can honestly list partial RFC slices as shipped

### When to split vs nest

| Situation | Action |
|-----------|--------|
| Same feature, shipped in chunks across versions | **One RFC** — slices/phases inside |
| Different subsystem, independent ship/cancel | **Separate RFCs** (e.g. sync vs watch party) |
| Release theme / milestone index | **Meta RFC** (e.g. v1.2 bundle) — links to child RFCs; spec stays in each child |
| Concrete bug, test gap, debt with own fix | **Child issue** (parent links 019–022 pattern) |
| “Ship this slice in 0.7.7” | **Backlog Shipped row** linking to RFC/issue ID |

**Do not** invent IDs outside the prefixes in [Progress tracker format](#progress-tracker-format-mandatory--all-layers). Migration `P2-XX` IDs stay in migration docs only.

**Do not:** clone an RFC for the next version; put semver in RFC filenames; use `[canceled]` when you mean deferred to next version.

---

## On status change

1. Rename file (tag + move to terminal folder when `done` / `fixed` / `canceled`)
2. Update `**Status:**` in body
3. Update the folder README index
4. Grep old path in `docs/` and fix links

## After code changes (mandatory — same turn)

When you land or materially advance work tied to a backlog version or RFC, **do not stop at code**. Update docs in the **same turn**:

1. **Backlog** — flip `B*-S*` rows; update glance; rename tag if lifecycle moved
2. **RFC** — flip `R*-C*` / `R*-A*` rows; update glance; `**Status:**` if terminal
3. **Issue** — flip `I*-A*` / `I*-T*` rows; update glance; filename tag if terminal
4. **Indexes** — RFC README **Progress**; issues README **Progress**; backlog README **Active**
5. **Cross-links** — grep old filename slug under `docs/` and fix

**Forbidden:** code shipped with task rows still ⬜; aggregate-only glance with no item table; checkbox lists parallel to emoji tables.

Skip only when the change is unrelated to any version/RFC (pure refactor, typo, tooling).

| Folder | Terminal folders | Terminal statuses |
|--------|------------------|-------------------|
| `backlog/` | `done/` · `canceled/` | `done` · `canceled` |
| `rfc/` | `fixed/` · `canceled/` | `fixed` · `canceled` |
| `issues/` | `fixed/` · `canceled/` | `fixed` · `canceled` |
| `migration/` | `fixed/` · `canceled/` | `fixed` · `canceled` |

## Migration (`docs/migration/`)

Engine migration phases — numbered `01`–`03`, not RFCs. Same [Progress tracker format](#progress-tracker-format-mandatory--all-layers).

### Filename tags

`[draft]` · `[open]` · `[partial]` · `[fixed]` (in `fixed/`) · `[canceled]` (in `canceled/`)

Pattern: `NN-[{status}]-slug.md` — e.g. `01-[fixed]-rust-engine.md`

| Body status | Filename | Location |
|-------------|----------|----------|
| `draft` | `NN-[draft]-….md` | Phase scoped, not started |
| `open` | `NN-[open]-….md` | Actively migrating |
| `partial` | `NN-[partial]-….md` | In progress |
| `fixed` | `NN-[fixed]-….md` | `docs/migration/fixed/` |
| `canceled` | `NN-[canceled]-….md` | `docs/migration/canceled/` |

All current phases (1–3) are **`fixed`** in `fixed/`. Index: [migration/README.md](../../docs/migration/README.md).
